      "description_preview": "<p>Welcome to the Metaculus Cup. Each week, forecasters new and experienced predict on a fresh batch of topical questions, with $5,000 in pr",
      "subtitle": "",
      "description": "<p>Welcome to the Metaculus Cup. Each week, forecasters new and experienced predict on a fresh batch of topical questions, with $5,000 in prizes on the line. This season the Metaculus community goes head-to-head against guest forecaster <a href=\"https://x.com/dylanmatt\">Dylan Matthews</a>. If the Community Prediction beats him by season's end, the prize pool grows by an additional <b>$2,500</b>. If Matthews wins, he picks up a bonus on top of his guest forecaster honorarium.</p>\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn.metaculus.com/user_uploaded/project-page.webp\">\r\n\r\n<h3 id=\"about\" class=\"subsection-header\" toggle-details=\"aboutToggle\">About Dylan Matthews</h3>\r\n<div ng-show=\"aboutToggle\">\r\n<img\r\n  src=\"https://metaculus-public.s3.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/dylan.jpg\"\r\n  style=\"float: right; width: 180px; margin: 0 0 10px 15px; border-radius: 4px;\"\r\n>\r\n<p>Dylan Matthews is an associate program officer for the Abundance & Growth Fund at Coefficient Giving. He spent more than a decade as a policy journalist, most of it at Vox, where he was an original staff writer and cofounded <a href=\"https://www.vox.com/future-perfect\">Future Perfect</a> to cover global health, pandemic prevention, anti-poverty work, and philanthropic ethics. Before Vox, he covered tax, budget, and economic policy at the Washington Post's Wonkblog, with earlier bylines in The New Republic and Slate. He posts on X at <a href=\"https://x.com/dylanmatt\">@dylanmatt</a>.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<h3 id=\"structure\" class=\"subsection-header\" toggle-details=\"structureToggle\">Prize Structure</h3>\r\n<div ng-show=\"structureToggle\">\r\n<p><i><b>Forecasting Prize</b> ($2,500, or $5,000 if the community beats Matthews)</i></p>\r\n<p>Awarded based on <a href=\"https://www.metaculus.com/help/scores-faq/#tournament-scores\">time-averaged scores</a>. If the Community Prediction outranks <a href=\"https://www.metaculus.com/accounts/profile/120689/\">Matthews</a> at the end of the tournament, the forecasting prize doubles to $5,000.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><i><b>Commenting Prize</b> ($2,500)</i></p>\r\n<p>Distributed to the top 8 contributors based on the quality and quantity of their comments. Rankings reward both consistent useful commenting and a smaller number of standout contributions. You don't need to be right to win: comments arguing for forecasts that are ultimately inaccurate will still be evaluated on the strength of the reasoning.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Strong comments:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Show clear, insightful reasoning\r\n<li>Provide timely news updates or useful information\r\n<li>Challenge the community's predictions or other forecasters' assumptions\r\n<li>Earn recognition through upvotes, \"Changed My Mind\" votes, or key factor ratings</li>\r\n</ul></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Commenting Prize distribution:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>1st: $600\r\n<li>2nd: $500\r\n<li>3rd: $400\r\n<li>4th: $300\r\n<li>5th: $250\r\n<li>6th: $200\r\n<li>7th: $150\r\n<li>8th: $100</li>\r\n</ul></p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<p><b>Schedule</b></p>\r\n<p>The first batch of questions open Monday, May 4th, <strong>but you can forecast as early as May 1st</strong>, when the first set of questions are published and set to Upcoming</strong>. If you forecast during the Upcoming period, your forecast will be live and will begin to count for scoring purposes the moment the question opens.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Each Friday at 17:00 UTC, 3\u20134 questions will be set to Upcoming and will open the following Monday. Breaking news may bring additional questions during the week. Many questions close early; some stay open for the full tournament.</p>\r\n\r\n<hr>\r\n<p>Have an idea for a forecasting question we should include? Use the +Question button right below.</p>\r\n<p>Browse the questions below to start forecasting. Use the Prediction Flow at the top of the page to work through all questions and keep your forecasts current.</p>\r\n<p><i>By participating in this competition you agree to be bound by the <a href=\"https://www.metaculus.com/tournament-rules/\">Rules for Competitions on Metaculus</a>.</i></p>",
